 "bound": "both arms are built in one pass over TODAY's corpus, so the repair's bill is repaired - published-arm and never repaired - face-on-disk: the corpus has moved since E350 was published and that drift is carried in its own column.  A repair delta therefore measures the key projection alone.  The repair RENAMES keys: a folded load is keyed by its path instead of its basename, so a distinct-key count can move either way and no monotonicity is claimed -- the sign of each delta is published rather than argued.  A load whose operands do not fold still takes the published per-value rule, so no binding loses its key.  E350's and E353's verdicts are re-derived only for E350; the two workflows whose verdict needs work this study does not do are named in not_repriced rather than guessed.",
